from common import *
it('KERNEL-0001','rule','3.0','All shape mathematics lives in one kernel library that never throws and never guesses: whole-cm coordinates, exact side-of-line tests, every new line snapped and checked, typed failure reasons instead of exceptions or garbage.',['§3 intro (plain words)'],'kernel',['@KernelResult','@snap','@orient2d'],['§4 every stage','§5.1 failure ladder','§7 edits'],['kernel'],summary_of=['@KernelResult','@snap','@orient2d'])
it('KERNEL-0002','rule','3.0','Every generation stage changes geometry only through transactions: a batch of changes accepted whole after its rules are checked, or rejected whole; this is what removes whole-map retries.',['§3 intro (plain words)','§3.3 (normative home)'],'kernel',['@batch'],['§4 every stage','§5 no whole-map retry'],['transaction'],summary_of=['@batch'])
it('KERNEL-0003','decision','3.1','Lattice, snapping and attraction are BUILT in-house; degenerate inputs specified by §3.2 and §3.6.',['§3.1 table row 1'],'kernel',['@rangeInvariant','@attractCm'],['@snap','@insertChain'],['lattice build decision'])
it('KERNEL-0004','decision','3.1','Exact predicates: orient2d BUILT (exact in doubles under the range invariant §3.2 (1)); incircle ADOPTED from robust-predicates 3.0.3 (Unlicense; J-K36), licence confirmed against the public registry (docs/validation/redteam-improve.md §5.1), version pinned and re-checked by §17.4 licence checker on every upgrade; pre-decided fallback if a future version fails: in-house BigInt incircle (exact, slower). incircle is adaptive and never on the topology path; ties by §3.2 (3), orientation and areas by §3.2 (6).',['§3.1 table row 2'],'kernel',['@rangeInvariant','§17.4 licence checker','J-K36 (rationale)'],['@area2','@floatTopology','§3.8 skeleton','@delaunator','§17.2 licence table'],['orient2d','incircle','robust-predicates'])
it('KERNEL-0005','decision','3.1','Planar subdivision (the §2.2 record) is BUILT as the core asset: struct-of-arrays with allocation-free hot loops, because in the NG 1.2.2 profile creating points (385-561 k calls) and intersecting lines (147-213 k calls) dominate (G-R7). Its transactions §3.3, insertion and slivers §3.6, storage §3.9, invariants §3.10.',['§3.1 table row 3'],'kernel (data shape owned by §2.2 model)',['§2.2 planar subdivision record','G-R7 finding'],['@batch','@insertChain','@arenaStorage','@invariants','§12 performance budgets'],['struct-of-arrays'])
it('KERNEL-0006','decision','3.1','Polygon booleans, buffers, offsets, insets and bands are BUILT on the kernel arrangement (§3.7; J-K4). Clipper2 (BSL-1.0) and polygon-clipping (MIT) serve as CI oracles only, shipped only under §3.7 fallback.',['§3.1 table row 4','§3.7 (home)'],'kernel',['@oneEngine'],['@oneEngine','§13 CI oracle tests','§17.2 licence table'],['Clipper2','polygon-clipping'])
it('KERNEL-0007','decision','3.1','Straight skeleton is BUILT (§3.8; J-K5, J-A21.31); none adopted: no permissive mature JS/TS skeleton meets §3.8 numeric contract; CGAL skeleton is GPL (rest LGPL), excluded by §17.4 permissive-only production closure (module licence the owner\'s, §17.3), and fails the stack and one-engine grounds (C++ is not the TypeScript kernel every host runs, D-4; no WASM kernel, §3.7; its doubles cannot be byte-identical to §3.8 validated construction).',['§3.1 table row 5'],'kernel',['§17.3','§17.4','D-4'],['@skeleton'],['CGAL'])
it('KERNEL-0008','decision','3.1','OBB, convex hull and largest inscribed rectangle BUILT: monotone chain + rotating calipers; LIR sampled deterministically over four candidate axes: OBB long axis, frontage normal, +45 deg and -45 deg (G-R13).',['§3.1 table row 6'],'kernel',[],['§4.7 plots and buildings (OBB/LIR callers)','V02 buildings'],['OBB','convex hull','largest inscribed rectangle'])
it('KERNEL-0009','rule','3.1','GEO-7 degenerate contract for OBB/hull/LIR: fewer than 3 distinct points or a collinear hull returns E_DEGENERATE (detail collinear), never ok with a zero extent, so no caller divides by a zero minor axis; callers branch on the typed result.',['§3.1 table row 6','§3.1 KernelError E_DEGENERATE comment'],'kernel',['KERNEL-0008'],['every OBB/hull caller','@E_DEGENERATE','§13 GEO-7 test'],['GEO-7 hull contract'])
it('KERNEL-0010','decision','3.1','Best-fit regular polygon regularFit BUILT (§3.4; J-A45.31): a ring of fewer than 3 vertices, of zero area, or whose first component vanishes (radius below 1 cm) returns E_DEGENERATE (detail fit); a clockwise ring is read in reverse; cosines, sines and angles through dmath (§6.5).',['§3.1 table row 7','§3.1 E_DEGENERATE comment','§3.4 regularFit (home)'],'kernel',['§6.5 dmath','@area2'],['@regularFit'],['regularFit build decision'])
it('KERNEL-0011','decision','3.1','Delaunay/Voronoi ADOPTED: delaunator (ISC), d3-delaunay (ISC); duplicate points merged first; used only for site sampling, Lloyd relaxation, field seeds and medial axes, never as the street source (the S4 routing lattice is hexLattice, §3.4).',['§3.1 table row 8'],'kernel',[],['§4 site sampling / Lloyd relaxation / field seeds / medial axes','§17.2 licence table'],['delaunator','d3-delaunay'])
it('KERNEL-0012','decision','3.1','Poisson-disc/blue noise BUILT: Bridson with k = 50 candidates, all evaluated, each drawn in the §8.10 candidate annulus (poisson.annulus) about its active point, on a torus (wrap-around tile) - the sampler of MFCG build 12710731, VG 1.6.9, NG 1.2.2 and Dwellings itch 17195045 as their code reads (P14; k = 50 measured by _critic.md C2; G-P17); run at PRODUCT BUILD TIME to make the §8.10 stamp tiles; per-instance placement by §8.1 (2) and §8.10. Domain clipped to any polygon with holes; an empty domain returns empty.',['§3.1 table row 9'],'kernel (stamp use owned by §8 rendering)',['§8.10 poisson.annulus table value','§6.1 streams'],['§8.10 stamp tiles','§8.1 (2) per-instance placement','KERNEL-0013'],['poisson','Bridson','poisson.annulus'])
it('KERNEL-0013','rule','3.1','A ragged wood edge comes from thinning the stamped points by the domain-warped density noise (§4.9), never from warping the Poisson sampler (COV-VG-WC3).',['§3.1 table row 9'],'§4.9 pipeline (greenery) / §8.10 rendering',['KERNEL-0012','KERNEL-0014'],['§4.9','§8.10'],['wood edge'],restates='§4.9 (home of the wood-edge rule)')
it('KERNEL-0014','decision','3.1','Noise (fBm, domain warp, ridged): simplex-noise (MIT) ADOPTED; seeding, fBm and warp BUILT; seeded from sub-streams (§6.1); octaves and lacunarity are table values (VG 5-octave field, _critic-vg-ng.md V7).',['§3.1 table row 10'],'kernel',['§6.1 sub-streams','@plat/tables noise rows'],['§4.1 S1 terrain','§4.9 density noise','§8 textures'],['simplex-noise','fBm'])
it('KERNEL-0015','decision','3.1','Curves BUILT: Chaikin, centripetal Catmull-Rom to cubic, pinned-vertex Laplacian, Visvalingam-Whyatt, circular fillets. Results re-enter through insertChain; smoothing committed geometry is a warp (§3.4, §3.6); Visvalingam-Whyatt is the topology-preserving simplify (§3.4); fillets are skipped when a leg is shorter than the chord.',['§3.1 table row 11'],'kernel',['@insertChain','@warp','@simplify'],['§4 road and shore smoothing','§8 render smoothing'],['Chaikin','Catmull-Rom','Visvalingam','fillet'])
it('KERNEL-0016','decision','3.1','Spatial index: flatbush (ISC) ADOPTED for static partitions plus a uniform grid per level (§3.3); rbush (MIT) only for the screen-space label collision index (§9).',['§3.1 table row 12'],'kernel (label index owned by §9)',[],['@indexRebuild','§9 label collision'],['flatbush','rbush'])
it('KERNEL-0017','decision','3.1','Marching squares ADOPTED (d3-contour, ISC; §17 licence table); distance transform BUILT, linear time. VG 1.6.9 costliest terrain routine (a field pushing roads and highway entrance away from water) is not reproduced - the S4 lattice crossing penalty (§4.3) keeps roads off water; VG grid-staircase coastlines smoothed in two passes and resampled are replaced by contour extraction; contours are extracted per render tile, not in S1, and are never plat edges (§2.3, §8).',['§3.1 table row 13'],'kernel (contour use owned by §8)',['§2.3 rasters'],['§8 contour rendering per tile','§4.3 S4 crossing penalty'],['d3-contour','marching squares','distance transform'])
